Z||000000||84 2in1||05-05-2001||08:02 PM||||I've run into many eletrical problims with my little car someone wired three seperate wires together at the battery post . My altenator is overchargeing and i fried one of my spare comps.Is there any where I can get a wire diagram to sort these wires out? My hanes manual is not very clear when it comes to their diagrams.Thanx in advance -B-||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-05-2001||09:06 PM||||Look for some aftermarket stuff that those wires might be going to.  Like a radio, an amp, or an alarm system.  The reason you arent finding the wires in any schematics is because they arent supposed to be there at all.  They are obviously for some aftermarket  stuff.  Disconnect them, and then see if your alternator is still overcharging.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||05-06-2001||08:31 AM||||You need the Pontiac service manual from Helms...<BR>Expensive, but worth it...<BR>Someone may have moved the wire from the starter to the battery, but without being there, it is just a guess...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
